  "slug": "validated-gene-ad03",
  "summary": "Updated variant evidence resources and truth-based pipeline validation frameworks appear together in recent preprints and a published database update.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is infrastructure linking variant evidence to clinical interpretation. MetaDome 2027 (published) aggregates missense population and pathogenic evidence across homologous Pfam domains, with GRCh38 support. memVar (preprint) integrates roughly 10.9M ClinVar, COSMIC and gnomAD SNVs across 7,732 membrane proteins, annotated with topology, lipid contacts and interaction data. A second preprint presents an end-to-end in silico framework that tests clinical sequencing pipelines against planted truth variants, from simulated reads to reportable findings, for regression testing. PRISM applies an agentic LLM pipeline to 3.9M online health community posts to surface ClinVar reinterpretation needs and draft outreach. What is new is the move from static resource building toward systematic detection of where interpretation and pipeline performance fail, whether in curated databases, sequencing workflows, or patient-generated text.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
